+::a26b1 This answer is bound to the first entry of that list, and it is a contribution in its own right. ::a26b2 Because it refers to segment `a26`, its key is `a26b`, and its own segments are keyed `a26b1`, `a26b2`, and so on.
+
+::a26b3 What that arrangement enables:
+
+- ::a26b4 An answer appears directly underneath the segment it refers to. ::a26b5 **A segment is therefore tied to its context twice — by its key and by the place where it is shown.** Whole levels of answers can be folded away when a page gets crowded.
+- ::a26b6 An answer is set apart from the surrounding contribution by colour and indentation, such that readers always know the text of which party they are reading.
+- ::a26b7 Any number of parties can take part, each with its own letter. ::a26b8 By the way, that letter becomes part of the key of any contribution by that party (see the example below).
+- ::a26b9 Contributions may be written in Markdown.
+
+::a26b10 Because the context of an answer is by technical means tied to the segment, quoting any party out of context does not work. ::a26b11 The surrounding text (and thus the original context) is at most one click away.
\ No newline at end of file
